e board writes, so foreman board writes do not use the stale copy. The exposure is any other caller of the PATH binary (sibling projects boards, operator one-offs) running a build with neither the DF-6 knobs nor the BT-039 hygiene.\n6. Deliberately NOT re-done in this cycle: a manual re-copy of the binary. Two writers building and installing into a live board repo while its tick lane can build is how the dirty-mtime confusion (BT-039) recurs; the durable half is the verification + provenance step, which is this row.\nAC: (1) an install target or a documented install step that installs the RELEASED asset by tag and verifies sha256, so the deployed binary is reproducible from the tag and identifiable; (2) a stated verification probe (e.g. `boardctl version --json` expected value, or `go version -m`) in README/Development so drift is detectable at any time, not just during a release audit; (3) after the next release, a probe shows the deployed binary reporting the released tag with vcs.modified=false and a revision that is an ancestor of that tag — quote the probe output; (4) the next cycle that re-cuts a release notes whether the installed copy moved, so this class gets a signal instead of a rediscovery.", "created_at": "2026-09-21T13:07:08Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T22:49:49Z", "worker_status": "pending", "detail": {"fingerprint": "637955a0964ae5ed87a200d77bd0672ad6f13b57a2ff1a7a256398c5b864894a"}, "ts": null, "complexity": 2, "foreman_note": null, "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/boardctl-BT-042", "branch": "wt/BT-042", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "sessions": null, "completed_at": null, "capability_tags": ["deploy", "install", "stale"]}
 {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-8", "title": "Burndown renders 2 of 20 points on v0.1.7 — the DF-BOARDCTL-1 fix passes x-labels (window bounds) as the x array, so linePath draws a two-point stub and silently discards the real open series", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-09-22 (dogfood run, fleet/multi-board angle; release binary v0.1.7, checksum-verified).\nREPRO: boardctl -C . render -o /tmp/r.html (this repo board, 20-day burndown window).\nEVIDENCE: payload derived.burndown = {window:[2026-09-03, 2026-09-22] (2 bounds), open:[2,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,5,4,2,1,1,0,0,9,1,2,2] (20 values)}; template.go:714 calls chartLines(bd, [{days: d.burndown.window, values: d.burndown.open}...]) — window is [start,end], not per-day labels. chartLines derives xs from series[0].days (2 entries), and linePath (internal/render/template.go:348) loops xs.length, so the drawn path is M30.00 117.33 L452.00 132.67 — 2 of 20 points, verified by executing the report's own chartLines/linePath under node with a DOM stub. The 9-open spike and the whole real series never render. Worse than the v0.1.6 blank panel (DF-BOARDCTL-1): now the panel LOOKS correct — a plausible down-trending line instead of an obvious placeholder — while discarding 18 of 20 data points. Reproduced independently on a fresh Debian 13 bunker box from a fresh clone (burnup renders correctly: days is a real per-day array there).\nFIX DIRECTION: give BurndownSeries a real per-day labels array (mirror BurnupSeries.days, derive.go:41) and pass it at template.go:714 + the overlay site; add a payload-shape test asserting burndown.days.length === burndown.open.length (the missing gate this bug class keeps slipping through).", "created_at": "2026-09-22T13:58:05Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T06:22:56Z", "worker_status": "done", "detail": {"fingerprint": "95c5312ada5106c989bdc6061ad8e810ce628b1c5570557d28cffe3916f5a81c"}, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "foreman_note": "Merged 9b96380, pushed. Post-merge full suite gr