 {"id":"DF-BOARDCTL-14","title":"P2 — install + board-lint hook (BT-054) is absent from --help usage text and the usage-closure meta-test did not catch it","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-24T18:50:00+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"OBSERVED 2026-09-24 (dogfood run 15). `boardctl --help` lists 16 commands; `install` is not among them, and `boardctl install` responds to -h with the correct one-line usage. The BT-054 commit message says 'The usage-closure meta-test's pinned count 15 -> 16' — the count was bumped when sweep-status landed, but install is a 17th command living outside the closure (or the closure walker has a gap). A user discovering the hook feature has no way to find it from the CLI itself; the feature is discoverable only by reading commit history. Reproduced with both the dev binary (bin/boardctl) and the released v0.1.8 asset. FIX DIRECTION: add install to the usage text; make the usage-closure meta-test walk the actual command switch (main.go cases) instead of a pinned count so a new case cannot ship undocumented again.","detail":{"fingerprint":"dg15-df-boardctl-14-install-help"},"complexity":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-25T21:57:24+00:00","capability_tags":[],"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"b9a57bd","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Usage-closure meta-test now DERIVES the expected command set from run()'s switch in main.go (shape-based: a case printing usageText directly owns no fs.Usage closure) and attributes every closure via the latest-newFlagSet(<verb>)-before-closure rule; pinned want:=16 removed; negative-control test (TestUsageClosureGateNegativeControl) proves a closure-less synthetic command FAILS the gate naming it. Tests TestUsageClosureGateDerivesFromCommandSwitch + negative control PASS; full go test -count=1 ./... green on merged tree (8 ok); worker commit 9f4eb67 (+386/-10, test-only), merged b9a57bd, CI green on push.","foreman_note":"Row premise was PARTIALL