 {"id":"DF-BOARDCTL-15","title":"P2 — skills/boardctl-usage/SKILL.md (v1.5.0) predates the two newest subcommands: sweep-status and install are absent from the agent-facing entry-points section","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-24T18:50:00+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"OBSERVED 2026-09-24 (dogfood run 15). The in-repo usage skill is what teaches future agents this CLI; its entry-points list stops at the pre-BT-054 surface — `sweep-status` (landed 2026-09-24, REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001) and `install` (board-lint pre-commit hook, BT-054) appear nowhere in the file, and the version pin stays 1.5.0. README.md DOES document sweep-status (line 251) but not install. An agent loading the skill would use validate --repair where sweep-status --apply is now the sanctioned write path, or would never learn the hook exists. FIX DIRECTION: bump the skill to 1.6.0: add both commands with their exit contracts (sweep-status exits 0 in BOTH modes — census is a finding, not a failure; install --dry-run prints the hook block), plus the run-15 verification results. Docs-only fix.","detail":{"fingerprint":"dg15-df-boardctl-15-skill-stale"},"complexity":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T23:35:47+00:00","capability_tags":[],"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"1e09d45","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Wave worker glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm: skill-freshness gate (TestUsageSkillCoversEveryTopLevelCommand parses the real usageText constant — same string --help prints — and asserts every top-level command appears in Entry points OR Proven commands; gate caught real drift on first run: render/import/serve documented only in Report surface, now added, skill bumped 1.6.0->1.7.0; TestSkillCoverageParserProvesGatesBite pins the extractor to 16 commands; negative probes: sweep-status stripped / fake zz-newcmd both FAIL naming the missing command). Judge round 1 FAIL (criterion 3: header date unasserted) -> fixup worker wt/DF-BOARDCTL-15-fix: f