 {"id":"BT-064","title":"P2 — boardctl create GLUED a new row onto an unterminated last line, corrupting BOTH rows","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-25T13:09:05+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"appendBytes (internal/board/write.go) wrote straight through O_APPEND with no terminator check. Appending to a\nboard whose last line has no trailing newline put the new row on the SAME line: every line-based reader then sees\none malformed row ('Extra data' from any JSON parser) and BOTH ids disappear - silent data loss, no error, exit 0.\nObserved live on 2026-09-25: heading INT-CI-2693 landed glued to the row before it and had to be split back apart\nbyte-exact by hand (all 157 pre-existing lines verified unchanged afterwards).\nFixed: ensureTrailingNewline() normalizes the last byte before every append (absent/empty files untouched,\nterminated files byte-identical). Regression test internal/board/bt064_append_newline_test.go (RED before the fix:\n'want 2 lines, got 1 - the rows were glued'; GREEN after) plus the new-file and terminated-file edge cases.\nCommit 017577b, full suite green, binary installed and re-proven live: header + 2 rows on a deliberately\nunterminated file -> 3 lines, 3 parseable.","detail":{"fingerprint":"180f2e1bc40f086058ca847198be5beba6bd0e8660f158a7d8f5163f87ab68c9"},"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-25T13:09:05+00:00","capability_tags":[],"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":"017577b","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"fixed in 017577b; RED->GREEN test + live proof on the installed binary","foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"sessions":null,"depends_on":[],"worktree":null,"branch":null}
